        "comments": "The assembly of Trachinus draco (fTraDra6) is based on 44X PacBio data and 279X OmniC Hi-C data generated as part of the ATLASea programme (https://www.atlasea.fr). The assembly process included the following steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, removal of contaminant sequences using Context, removal of haplotypic duplications using purge_dups, and Hi-C-based scaffolding with YaHS. No contigs were found to be contaminants (bacterial, archaeal, or viral). Additionally, 172 regions totaling 30.625 Mb (with the largest being 8.654 Mb) were identified as haplotypic duplications and removed. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analyzed and manually improved using Pretext. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by Hi-C data were named in order of size.",
